        "object": "<ul><li><p>Former Port Adelaide coach will prepare club for 2028 entry</p></li><li><p>Nathan Buckley and John Longmire overlooked for role</p></li></ul><p>Ken Hinkley has been officially named as the Tasmania Devils’ inaugural AFL coach, less than 12 months after being <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/aug/20/from-the-pocket-ken-hinkleys-farewell-tour-ends-with-results-clouding-whether-his-reign-was-a-success\">moved on from Port Adelaide</a>.</p><p>The league’s newest expansion franchise, who will enter the competition in 2028, announced on Monday that the 59-year-old had signed a five-year deal.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/20/ken-hinkley-coach-tasmania-devils-afl\">Continue reading...</a>"
